  "question": "1) Background / Context\n\nThe project aims to develop a real-time messaging and conversation system, \"Talk,\" specifically designed for integration into Laravel-based applications. This system enables seamless communication between users by facilitating real-time chat functionality, enhancing user engagement within any Laravel project.\n\n 2) Objectives\n\n- Develop a user-friendly, real-time messaging system for Laravel applications.\n- Support head-to-head messaging between users.\n- Enable easy integration into existing Laravel projects.\n- Provide essential functionalities to manage conversations and message threads effectively.\n\n 3) Stakeholders & Users\n\n- Primary Users: End-users of any Laravel-based application integrating the messaging system, who require real-time communication capabilities.\n- Developers: Individuals or teams responsible for integrating and maintaining the messaging system within their Laravel projects.\n- Administrators: Personnel responsible for overseeing the operations and integrity of the messaging system in each application.\n\n 4) Functional Descriptions\n\n- Real-time Messaging: Users can send and receive messages instantaneously.\n- Conversation Management: \n  - Create new conversations between users.\n  - Access message threads, displaying the latest messages.\n  - Support pagination for viewing extensive threads and messages.\n- Message Controls:\n  - Soft delete messages, allowing both sender and receiver to remove messages from their perspective.\n  - Permanently delete messages, removing them entirely.\n  - Mark messages as seen, indicating they have been read by the recipient.\n- Access Control: Only conversation participants can view and manage their respective messages and threads.\n- OEmbed Integration: Inline rendering of URLs within messages, following oEmbed specifications.\n\n 5) Non-Functional Descriptions\n\n- Scalability: The system should efficiently handle user growth and increased messaging volume.\n- Performance: Ensure low latency in message delivery and retrieval to maintain real-time communication.\n- Reliability: Implement robust mechanisms for message delivery, even under high load or network fluctuations.\n- Security: Protect user data and communication through secure message handling and access control protocols.\n- Usability: Ensure the system is intuitive and easily navigable for end-users, promoting seamless integration into existing user interfaces.",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: schemabench_0060\nCREATE TABLE `conversations` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `created_at` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `updated_at` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `conversation_participants` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `conversation_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `last_read_message_id` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `deleted_at` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `created_at` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `updated_at` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  UNIQUE KEY `conversation_participants_unique` (`conversation_id`,`user_id`),\n  KEY `conversation_participants_ibfk_2` (`user_id`),\n  KEY `conversation_participants_ibfk_3` (`last_read_message_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `conversation_participants_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`conversation_id`) REFERENCES `conversations` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `conversation_participants_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `users` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `conversation_participants_ibfk_3` FOREIGN KEY (`last_read_message_id`) REFERENCES `messages` (`id`) ON DELETE SET NULL ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `messages` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `conversation_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `sender_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `body` text NOT NULL,\n  `seen_at` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `deleted_at` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `created_at` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `updated_at` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  KEY `messages_ibfk_1` (`conversation_id`),\n  KEY `messages_ibfk_2` (`sender_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `messages_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`conversation_id`) REFERENCES `conversations` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `messages_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`sender_id`) REFERENCES `users` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `message_oembeds` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `message_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `url` varchar(2048) NOT NULL,\n  `provider_name` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `provider_url` varchar(2048) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `title` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `type` varchar(50) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `html` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `thumbnail_url` varchar(2048) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `width` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `height` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `created_at` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `updated_at` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  KEY `message_oembeds_ibfk_1` (`message_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `message_oembeds_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`message_id`) REFERENCES `messages` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
